00:41:45,600 --> 00:41:51,600
This page documents notable tornadoes and tornado outbreaks worldwide in 2009.

13
00:45:14,400 --> 00:45:20,400
Strong and destructive tornadoes form most frequently in the United States, Argentina, Brazil,
Bangladesh, and Eastern India, but can occur almost anywhere under the right conditions.

14
00:48:43,200 --> 00:48:49,200
Tornadoes also develop occasionally in southern Canada during the Northern Hemisphere's summer and somewhat
regularly at other times of the year across Europe, Asia, Argentina, Australia and New Zealand.

15
00:52:12,000 --> 00:52:18,000
Tornadic events are often accompanied by other forms of severe weather,
including strong thunderstorms, strong winds, and hail.

16
00:55:40,800 --> 00:55:46,800
In the U.S., there were 1,304 reports of tornadoes received by the Storm
Prediction Center, and 1,159 tornadoes were confirmed to have taken place.

17
00:59:09,600 --> 00:59:15,600
Worldwide, 73 fatalities were caused by tornadoes; 22 in the United States, 20 in India, 11 in Argentina, eight in
the Philippines, four each in Canada and Brazil, two in Greece and one each in Serbia and Russia.

18
01:02:38,400 --> 01:02:44,400
Tornadic activity in 2009 began with the development an EF1 tornado near Stringer, Mississippi on January 3
and ended with the dissipation of an EF0 tornado near Vancleave, Mississippi on December 24.

19
01:06:07,200 --> 01:06:13,200
During the year the two strongest tornadoes were both assessed as an EF4 – one occurred in
Oklahoma on February 10 and the second occurred in Tennessee on April 10.

20
01:09:36,000 --> 01:09:42,000
During the early months of the year tornadic activity remained mostly below
average in contrast to an active trend of tornadoes in 2008.

21
01:13:04,800 --> 01:13:10,800
Activity peaked in April and May as a result of destabilizing atmospheric
conditions and featured a bulk of the year's tornadoes.

22
01:16:33,600 --> 01:16:39,600
However, the number of developing tornadoes subsequently began to wane and
remained generally inactive for the latter half of 2009.

23
01:20:02,400 --> 01:20:08,400
The film explores themes of farm, tornado, widower, disaster movie.

24
01:23:31,200 --> 01:23:37,200
The tone is intense and emotional and mind_bending.
